WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:02.280
I'm in charge here.
I'm the captain.

00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:03.600
Wow!

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:06.760
This is Superfan
vs. Super Fan:

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.400
Stranger Things Edition.

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:09.680
Hello, and welcome here

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:11.720
to the windy city
of Manchester.

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:12.880
I'm Munya Chawawa,

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:14.920
here to take
two Netflix superfans

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.760
through a whirlwind
of blistering challenges

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:19.240
and gale-force knowledge.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:20.200
But how does it work?

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:22.480
Well, I'm glad
you asked, Munya.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:25.040
Our Netflix superfans
go head to head

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:26.040
answering questions

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:27.960
about their favourite
Netflix shows

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:29.800
from these living rooms.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:32.600
And if they get
a question right,

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:34.240
they move up this board,

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:35.360
slowly edging their way

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:37.440
towards
ultimate super fandom.

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:40.640
But they won't just be
battling against each other.

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:41.520
Oh no.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:43.280
Each superfan
has also to withstand

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:45.400
these super fans...

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:46.560
How powerful are they?

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:50.720
Well, David,
given a blustery 20mph,

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:53.280
but every three questions
a superfan gets right

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:55.160
will increase
their opponent's fan speed

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:58.440
until it reaches 100mph.

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:01.320
But what happens
when it reaches 100mph?

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:05.040
Well, then,

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.640
that superfan
will get super flanned.

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:10.600
Oh, right. Okay.

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:13.920
And I will be controlling
the entire show from here,

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.080
the cockpit
of Chair Force One.

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:18.880
I'm the captain
and whatever I say blows.

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:20.600
So show me some respect.

00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:23.280
Okay.

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:25.080
I'm just…
I'll hop into here.

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:26.320
One, two, three!

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:27.840
Today,
we're flaying the minds

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:30.160
of two
Stranger Things superfans.

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:31.680
One will end
on a Hawkins high

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:34.800
and the other will be saying
bye, bye, Byers!

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:37.560
But enough of me
waffling on.

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:39.040
What am I, an Eggo?

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:40.480
Let's meet the superfans.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:43.360
Lily is a radio DJ
from Gosport.

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:44.320
A self-confessed nerd,

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:45.640
she has an "Eleven" tattoo

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:47.520
and loves
her Stranger Things Lego.

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:48.400
Once in Southsea,

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:49.760
Lily got knocked
off her feet

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:51.280
by the wind
from a hovercraft.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:53.320
She said
she laughed hysterically.

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:55.440
I've got an Eleven tattoo
on the front of my hand,

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:57.680
but I'll now show off
the back...

00:01:58.200 --> 00:01:59.360
Of my hand. That's...

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:03.080
Alexis is a belly dancer
from Wolverhampton.

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:04.920
She loves the nostalgia
of the series,

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.120
is a sucker for merch,

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:07.480
and her Eleven figurine

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:09.680
takes pride of place
on her car dashboard.

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:12.800
Her favourite genre of fan
is oscillating guest.

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:15.160
Lily might be
the stranger thing,

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:16.800
but I'm the stronger thing.

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:20.920
Welcome to the show,
the superfans!

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.080
I know it's all smiles
and giggles at the moment,

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:24.440
sharing muesli
in the greenroom.

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:25.720
This is not
the place for that.

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:28.480
Any trash talk before
we get into the competition?

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:30.600
-I'm gonna take her down!
-Ooh!

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:32.200
I could feel
the venom pouring out,

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:33.800
like a deadly
Demogorgon sting.

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:34.680
Lily?

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:36.120
I'm gonna take her
to the Upside Down.

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:38.840
Ooh, you don't
wanna go there. Ask Barb.

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:41.640
Well, the fans
are all in place.

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:42.760
It's time to play
and find out

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:44.480
which one of you
is a Silly Billy

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:46.800
and which of you
is a Dr. Smartin Brenner.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:48.560
On your marks...

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:51.040
get set...

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:53.000
blow!

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:56.760
Fangers on buzzers

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:58.640
as we jump
into question number one...

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:01.920
Who gives Eleven her
nickname 'EL'?

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:02.800
Mike.

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:04.800
…is the correct answer.

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:07.400
Maya Hawke, who plays Robin,
is the daughter of…?

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:08.480
Ethan Hawke.

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:11.160
…is the incorrect answer.

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:13.480
The full question was, "Maya
Hawke, who plays Robin,

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:14.600
is the daughter
of Ethan Hawke

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:15.840
and which actress?"

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:17.520
It was Uma Thurman.

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:20.280
So, I'm gonna have to
be robbin' a point off you,

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:21.360
if you'll pardon the pun!

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:23.760
Featuring in the comedy
series Fleabag,

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:25.760
who does Brett Gelman play
in Strange--

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:27.840
Murray.

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:29.240
Well, Alexis, you said
"Murray" in a hurry

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:30.120
and it paid off,

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:31.600
which means, Lily,

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:33.120
you're about
to get a bit more chilly.

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:35.400
Gonna crank up that fan.
Here we go.

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:40.680
Describe the sensations
you're experiencing now.

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:41.720
Windy.

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:43.240
Windy?
Yes, I know the feeling.

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:45.280
Those tikka masalas
will do that to a man.

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:48.200
Right now, it's time for the
Upside Down Picture Game.

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:51.160
So, to start us off,

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:52.720
who is this?

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:55.960
-Nancy Wheeler.
-It certainly is.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:58.160
Nancy was looking
very fancy there.

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:00.400
Over to the next one.
Who is this?

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:03.160
Bob Newby.

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:04.680
Goodness me!
Is your name Gale?

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:06.880
Because you are a force
to be reckoned with.

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:11.440
Which key character is
played by actor Mark Steger?

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:14.920
I'm gonna go with...

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:16.840
Murray? I don't know.

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:19.720
Now, it is
the incorrect answer,

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:20.800
but you know what?

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:22.080
This show
is all about effort.

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:23.720
So you get a point, Lily.

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:26.040
You're joking!
You're joking, aren't you?

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:27.480
Alexis, how does that feel?

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:29.560
I think I've remembered
who it is.

00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:30.640
-Go on.
-It's kind of annoying.

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:31.960
The Demogorgon?

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:34.320
Oh, Alexis,
too little, too late!

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:35.960
Shout out to my girl JoJo!

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:37.080
Right, now,
you might have heard

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:39.400
of the 80s
board game Dingbats...

00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:40.560
I know I haven't.

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:41.800
Now it's time
for our version,

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:43.160
Stranger Thingbats,

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:45.360
the wordplay catchphrase
game nobody asked for!

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:48.000
I'm gonna
show you a picture.

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:50.080
Flay your mind
and flay what you see.

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:51.360
Let's see the first one.

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:55.120
Free falling?

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:56.480
Ooh! It's not.

00:04:56.560 --> 00:04:59.120
The answer I was looking for
was "mic drop".

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:00.800
-Ah!
-See a mic being dropped?

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:02.840
We're very literal
with this game, okay?

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:04.760
Don't ever question
my Photoshop skills.

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:06.720
I mean, ten out of ten.

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:07.960
Eleven out of ten.
Am I right?

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:08.880
Eleven out of ten.

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:10.840
Mouth breather.

00:05:10.920 --> 00:05:13.160
And I'm gonna have to get
Crank McCrankyson right now,

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:14.560
because your fan
is going up.

00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:18.240
Right. Fingers on buzzers
for the next one.

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:20.320
So, who can you see?

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:22.800
Yes?

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:24.720
-Space Hopper.
-Correct answer!

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:25.920
Well done, Lily.

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:28.720
Okay, back to Quizzness.
Here we go.

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:31.360
What arcade game
do the gang play

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:33.040
at the start of season two,

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:35.440
where they have to save
Princess Daphne?

00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:37.680
Is it Dragon Quest?

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:39.280
Oh...

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:44.000
Lily, you were so close.
It was Dragon's Lair.

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:46.840
And that means another point
is heading over to Alexis.

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:47.800
Let me tell you,

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:50.560
if you had a hat, a whip
and a PhD in Archaeology,

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:52.120
you'd be Windyana Jones.

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:55.600
Right, now, sometimes,

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:57.240
Hopper likes
to tell a little porky.

00:05:57.320 --> 00:05:58.600
Cheeky!

00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:00.560
I'm gonna give you a series
of true or false questions,

00:06:00.640 --> 00:06:02.520
and all you need to do
is tell me whether it's true

00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:04.080
or a Hopper's Whopper.

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:05.080
Let's see the first one.

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:08.720
Stranger Things
is set in the 1970s.

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:11.280
-Alexis?
-Hopper's Whopper.

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:12.520
-It's false.
-It is, indeed.

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:15.720
And that answer was breezy
like a Sunday morning.

00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:18.520
Right, here's another one…
True or Hopper's Whopper?

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:20.920
Bob Newby dresses
as a mummy for Hallow--

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:23.080
It's a Whopper, as well.

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:24.360
Go on.
What's the correct answer?

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:26.720
-He dresses as a vampire.
-Absolutely.

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:27.600
And let me tell you,

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:29.000
that really sucks
for you, Lily,

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:30.960
because that means Alexis
has got another point,

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:32.720
and I'm gonna
have to crank up the fan.

00:06:36.760 --> 00:06:38.520
You're feeling more of
a breeze now, are you?

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:39.440
Just a little bit.

00:06:39.520 --> 00:06:40.920
Okay, well,
you'd better hurricane

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:41.840
and get back in the game,

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:44.120
because it's time for
another Stranger Thingbat.

00:06:44.600 --> 00:06:47.840
Ladies, tell me what you see
on screen right now.

00:06:49.560 --> 00:06:51.280
-Yes, Lily?
-Max volume.

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:53.920
…is the correct answer.
Air high five!

00:06:55.240 --> 00:06:57.320
Lily, you answered that
just in the nick of time,

00:06:57.880 --> 00:06:59.240
which means, Alexis,

00:06:59.320 --> 00:07:00.840
your fan
is about to get cranked.

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:05.920
Okay, so it's time

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:07.640
for some more
Hoppers Whoppers.

00:07:07.720 --> 00:07:09.720
Is this true
or a Hopper's Whopper?

00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:13.080
Season three
has the most epis--

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:14.400
False.

00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:17.920
Dustin has a remote
controlled R2D2--

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:18.960
True.

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:20.640
…is the correct answer.

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:22.640
Time for some more
Stranger Thingbats.

00:07:22.720 --> 00:07:24.760
Have a look on the screen
and flay what you see.

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:28.440
-Yes?
-Barbed wire.

00:07:28.520 --> 00:07:30.640
…is the correct answer.
Well played, Lily.

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:32.320
Here's another
Stranger Dingbat.

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:37.040
-Lily?
-Is it "neighbour"?

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:39.600
Ooh, no, no, it's not.

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:41.760
-It was "Mayornaise".
-Ah!

00:07:41.840 --> 00:07:44.200
I'm gonna have
to crank up your fan. Sorry!

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:51.000
Oh, boy. Now, it's looking
quite intense down there.

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:53.040
It is quite intense,
to be honest.

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:54.880
Alexis, looking calm and
collected there on the left.

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:56.200
A bit smug, actually.

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:58.080
Anyway, it's time
to check the scores

00:07:58.160 --> 00:07:59.960
so let's break wind.

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:02.240
How are we feeling, Lily?

00:08:02.320 --> 00:08:04.040
I'm trying to stay positive.

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:06.040
Go on. Give your little
Eleven tattoo a pep talk.

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:07.400
We can't be pied
in the face.

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:08.280
No, we can't.

00:08:08.360 --> 00:08:09.960
Come on. She's been
through enough already.

00:08:10.040 --> 00:08:11.800
She's gonna get a nosebleed
at this rate.

00:08:12.320 --> 00:08:13.720
Okay, guys,
let's stop gassing,

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:14.960
because wind the end,

00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:16.680
it all comes down to points.

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:18.120
However,
I'll tell you this...

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:20.000
I'm in the mood
for double points.

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:21.280
Ooh!

00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:26.160
Fangers on buzzers, please,
for the next question.

00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:28.920
What colour is the door to
the basement bunker

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:32.160
that Dustin traps his pet
Demogorgon D'Artagnan in,

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:33.280
in season two?

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:35.120
-Blue.
-Ooh…

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:36.560
It is actually red,

00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:37.720
which means, Lily,

00:08:37.800 --> 00:08:39.080
you're not only
getting one point,

00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:39.960
you're getting two.

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:41.040
I'd only do
something like that

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:42.880
for someone who's bribed me
before the show.

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:44.120
Going up two means

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:47.920
we must now
crank up Alexis' fan.

00:08:49.120 --> 00:08:50.560
A little push there.

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:52.440
Alexis, you are
blowing up in the world.

00:08:52.520 --> 00:08:54.520
Let's move
onto the next question.

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:57.960
What tabletop game are the
boys playing at the start--

00:08:58.040 --> 00:08:59.120
Dungeons and Dragons.

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:00.800
Is the correct answer,

00:09:00.880 --> 00:09:02.600
which means you go
up another point.

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:05.040
What is the name of Hawkins'
new shopping mall

00:09:05.120 --> 00:09:05.920
in season three?

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:07.760
Star Mall.

00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:08.720
Oh…

00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:11.840
Lily… you're gonna be
kicking yourself.

00:09:11.920 --> 00:09:13.440
I know I am.

00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:15.320
Star Court Mall.

00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:18.040
What shall we say?
Shall we give her the point?

00:09:18.520 --> 00:09:20.360
Just give them
a point anyway.

00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:21.360
I'm gonna give you a point,

00:09:21.440 --> 00:09:22.440
because
I am that kind of guy,

00:09:22.520 --> 00:09:24.360
which means
you are now on seven.

00:09:24.440 --> 00:09:25.680
Which British singer

00:09:25.760 --> 00:09:28.080
is Hopper actor
David Harbour married to?

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:30.920
-Lily Allen.
-Is the correct answer!

00:09:31.400 --> 00:09:33.120
Goodness me, you've clawed
another one back.

00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:35.920
I thought you were gonna be
Silly Allen, but no siree!

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:38.920
Which of the gang's
last name is Sinclair?

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:41.520
-Lucas.
-Lucas is correct.

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:45.440
Who did Steve put down as
a reference on his resumé--

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:46.640
His mum.

00:09:46.720 --> 00:09:48.760
The correct answer
was his mama.

00:09:48.840 --> 00:09:50.440
Which means, Alexis,

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:52.560
you've just grabbed
yourself another point,

00:09:52.640 --> 00:09:55.440
and Lily,
your fan is getting cranked

00:09:55.520 --> 00:09:56.600
to the next dimension.

00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:00.160
Ooh.

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:03.240
Alexis, you are now just
three short points away

00:10:03.320 --> 00:10:04.800
from being a super fan,
